Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||07-12-2000||02:13 AM||||well, I am in So. California and i need a new engine. i have a 1987 gt 5spd, and my 2.8 feels like it is getting a little tired. i am kinda lacking on the compression test, my mileage recently is failing, runs rich, gets water in the oil... I am very interested in the idea of a 3.4... whats the closest place to me that would be able to install a 3.4 for me and make it work? i was going to contact fiero motorsports but i cannot get ahold of them. where is chris west located? anyways, what kind of costs would i be looking at, what kinda stuff should i look for, and would a regular old engine shop be able to put the 3.4 in my car? i would try to do this all myself, but i must admit i do not have the greatest confidence, also, this car is my only transportation. i could get off work for maybe 4 days in a row, and i know i cannot do it myself that quickly. anyways, to summarize, anyone nearby that i could talk to about performing an engine swap, or at least getting a fresh 2.8 (installed) for a reasonable price? thanks much! (stupid ca smog....)||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||07-12-2000||12:57 PM||||I have a shop in the S.F. area. I've been doing 3.4 swaps. Fiero motorsports are no longer in business. Chris West is in Marine del Rey.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||07-12-2000||03:00 PM||||How come the majority of the cool shops are in cali? I mean, there's horrid emisions codes out there. There is a severe shortage of Fiero friendly shops on the east coast. it's about 10 hours to Fiero Bob's, and 8 hours to the Fiero Factory! How about a shop in Fredricksberg/Richmond VA? Just a way's south of DC, with out the high cost of living and a bunch of good ol'country boys wanting the best fiero available.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
